    {
      "card_ids": ["C05"],
      "claim": "In vivo, DMP696 occupied brain CRF1 receptors after oral dosing and brain concentrations exceeded plasma-free levels by >150-fold, directly demonstrating robust CNS access; this highest-transfer analogue strongly supports a pass for the query's similar chlorophenyl/fused heteroaromatic CRF1-antagonist-like scaffold.",
